    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 14-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate for dual-band filtering. Layer sequence: HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2 (14 finite layers total). Initialize thicknesses using the best configuration from prior iteration (candidate bragg_stack_opt__gradient_thickness__01) for central layers 5-10, and apply random offsets drawn from N(0, 8 nm) to outer layers 1-4 and 11-14. Set thickness bounds to ±20% relative tolerance around quarter-wave values at 550 nm reference. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with learning rate halved from default (step size reduced by 50%). Run 3 consecutive optimization cycles. Evaluate performance across 1530-1565 nm (maximize transmittance) and 400-700 nm (maximize reflectance) bands at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Incident medium is air. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica to maximize transmittance in 1530–1565 nm and reflectance in 400–700 nm at normal incidence, unpolarized illumination, subject to ±20% thickness tolerances via three gradient descent cycles.",
